WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:05.534
<v Captain>Muster the cadets! I want a headcount for every squadron.

2
00:00:06.184 --> 00:00:11.412
<v Alba>The Cadet table: 12 rows. COUNT(*) alone gives 12.

3
00:00:11.412 --> 00:00:16.471
<v Alba>The Captain wants one count for each squadron.

4
00:00:17.121 --> 00:00:21.606
<v Alba>GROUP BY squadronNo gathers rows with the same squadron number.

5
00:00:21.606 --> 00:00:23.850
<v Alba>Four squadrons, four groups.

6
00:00:24.500 --> 00:00:31.253
<v Alba>The aggregate runs once per group. Each group collapses into one row with its count.

7
00:00:31.903 --> 00:00:34.598
<v Alba>Add an alias for a readable heading,

8
00:00:34.598 --> 00:00:38.591
<v Alba>then ORDER BY COUNT(*) ASC for the smallest first.

9
00:00:38.791 --> 00:00:42.273
<v Alba>Remember: GROUP BY always comes before ORDER BY.

10
00:00:42.923 --> 00:00:45.618
<v Captain>Any traps for the unwary, Lieutenant?

11
00:00:45.818 --> 00:00:49.492
<v Alba>Two. An aggregate can't go in a WHERE clause:

12
00:00:49.492 --> 00:00:53.661
<v Alba>work it out in one query and use it in a second.

13
00:00:53.861 --> 00:00:58.604
<v Alba>And never mix a plain field with an aggregate unless you GROUP BY that field.

14
00:00:59.254 --> 00:01:02.894
<v Alba>Group, then aggregate, then order. Dismissed!

